  "worked_solution": "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={2}^{x} & \\,\u27f9\\,x={log}_{2}\u2061y \\\\ y=\\sqrt{x} & \\,\u27f9\\,x={y}^{2} \\\\ y=6-x & \\,\u27f9\\,x=6-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/fe95bc4ca8c687c79fe1c475eb1d8001d71a41ba34e076ad7fdfa8391cb08839.png)\n\n   \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/099c35cbab4dfdd4a94207ed950fbdca8b8e766a612fb5e665e7d443d75ec050.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,{log}_{2}\u2061y\\le x\\le {y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le y\\le 4,\\,{log}_{2}\u2061y\\le x\\le 6-y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\u222c}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{\u222c}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}\u2061y}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}\u2061y}^{6-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
